```cpp
bool operator"" _b(unsigned long long value);
    
bool x = 1_b;
```

Finding references on `_^b` does not give any references except itself. Reference to `_b` in `bool x = 1_b` is missing.

Similarly, `1_^b` gives no references at all.

This is confusing because UDLs are not visibly a function call.

```cpp
int inline consteval operator""_lit(unsigned long long val) { return 0; }

int main() {
    return 3_lit;
}
```

When the above is annotated by clangd, it puts `val: ` in front of `3_lit`, it looks like this:
```cpp
int main() {
    return val: 3_lit;
}
```

